<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ammaedara</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Haïdra</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ammaedara was a Roman town in the west of present-day <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tunisia">Tunisia</a>, at modern Haïdra near the Algerian border. It was the first base of the Third Augustan legion in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/africa">Africa</a>, set on the lands of the Musulamii, and became a colony of veterans when the legion moved to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tebessa">Theveste</a> under Vespasian. Its ruins include an arch, a Byzantine fortress and several churches.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ammaedara.jpg" alt="Ammaedara" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Astiosaurus · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Haidra_Tunisie.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
